{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788594160029011001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"stuffed-energistic-ladybird","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"474a1cff2cbab669e20787d5a60ed1c1a14abde2cf6e80d18e7faf0e485c3c57","event_uuid":"d11e286c-1c72-4216-bd7b-9d01028c2bb5","position":{"commit_sha":"a8376fe58662723304a840d53838a0acb3c413d5","position":"1788590193514084001-d11e286c-1c72-4216-bd7b-9d01028c2bb5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"dc0af22a80cf861ba1fa2ba1897527df346411a82030c1508c90c625ef7aa146","event_uuid":"086e817d-62d8-4625-a962-abcd62512c73","position":{"commit_sha":"8dddd93d3b212a7fb758404309466d397c431349","position":"1788590236481470001-086e817d-62d8-4625-a962-abcd62512c73"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3512d2e76fde9045b7adbe78f48a4e9395c7f7ddba5021ab7707ac28bb95f665","event_uuid":"3d38cc66-c82b-4a1d-9f9b-f642a3329ca0","position":{"commit_sha":"feb33b2efef6d2a81d193a020a5173bfa0d3585b","position":"1788590283526986001-3d38cc66-c82b-4a1d-9f9b-f642a3329ca0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## The fix direction is DEMONSTRATED, with an honest caveat\n\nRe-ran the same 9 files with a private slot directory — `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR=$(mktemp -d)`, so\nthe run gets its own `locks/` and its own 4 slots — while the four host-global slots stayed\noccupied by the other sessions listed in the description:\n\n```\n116 passed, 2 errors in 993.46s (0:16:33)\n```\n\n**Zero `GateCongestedError`.** Compare the same 9 files minutes earlier against the shared\nhost slot directory: `14 failed, 102 passed`, every failure `all 4 concurrent slots busy`.\nOne environment variable is the whole difference, which is as clean a confirmation of the\nmechanism as this is going to get.\n\n### The 2 errors are mine, not the suite's\n\n```\nERROR tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py::test_code_change_reruns_full_review\n  - Failed: The repo HEAD moved during this test (25d1d683e5 -> 8b2fee219f)\nERROR tests/unit/test_eval_solver.py::test_agentic_case_reroots_injected_runner_at_its_fixture\n  - Failed: The repo HEAD moved during this test (8b2fee219f -> 38396ebfcc)\n```\n\nThose two SHAs are my own commit and my own `make amend-msg`, run in that worktree while this\nverification was still in flight. The suite has a guard for exactly that and it fired\ncorrectly. So: not gate congestion, not a test defect, and not evidence for or against this\nticket — operator error on my part, recorded here rather than quietly dropped, because a\nreader comparing \"116 passed, 2 errors\" against my \"zero failures\" claim deserves to know\nwhich two and why.\n\nIt is also the second time in one session that acting on the tree during a long run polluted\nthe run. Cheap lesson, stated for the record: do not commit, amend, or edit inside a worktree\nthat has a suite running in it.\n\n### What this implies for the fix\n\nThe change needed is at the FIXTURE level, not in `gate_admission`: point `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR`\nat a per-session temp dir for the test suite. Production semantics stay exactly as they are —\na real gate op on a real host should contend for a genuinely shared, host-wide semaphore,\nwhich is the whole point of the design. Only the tests need to stop borrowing it.\n\n### Relationship to `torrential-unwhite-snail` (9c2e-b44c-119e-4105)\n\nRead that ticket before assuming this one supersedes it — it does not, and I want the record\nstraight rather than flattering. 9c2e already frames the cause cross-session (\"Any other\nsession on the machine holding gate slots — another agent running `review-plan` or a\ncompletion-gated close\"), and it already asks, in its own AC4, for \"a check that no other test\nin the suite has the same host-wide coupling, or a ticket filed for any that do\".\n\nSo this ticket is not a correction of 9c2e. It is the **answer to its AC4**, plus three things\n9c2e left open:\n\n1. the concrete code path (`_slot_dir()` -> `store_root()/locks` -> `tempfile.gettempdir()`),\n2. the scale (31 tests, 9 files, not 1), and\n3. the reason ordinary triage misleads here — admission fails closed WITHOUT waiting, so\n   re-running a test alone does not isolate it, and the holders can be processes running no\n   tests at all.\n\nIf anything is superseded it is the instinct to treat these as one-off flakes; the coupling is\nstructural and this is its inventory.","timestamp":1788590283526986001}],"created_at":1788590193514084001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"086e817d-62d8-4625-a962-abcd62512c73","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c2e-b44c-119e-4105"}],"description":"## What was observed\n\nA full `make verify` on 2026-09-04 in worktree `bug-9c93-ad8d-user-data-mounts` (a\n`user_data.sh` mount-assertion change, zero overlap with the LLM gate path) reported:\n\n```\n31 failed, 19489 passed, 75 skipped, 14 warnings in 4131.23s (1:08:51)\n```\n\n28 of the 31 were `rebar.llm.errors.GateCongestedError: gate admission refused: all 4\nconcurrent slots busy`. The other 3 (`tests/unit/test_plan_review_cli_retry.py`,\n`assert 11 == 2` on an LLM call count) were knock-on and passed in isolation.\n\n**Re-running the 9 affected files ALONE still produced 14 failures.** That is the finding:\n\"run it alone\" does not isolate this, so the usual triage step gives a FALSE \"this is real\nand it is mine\" verdict.\n\n## The mechanism\n\n`rebar.llm.gate_admission._slot_dir()` returns `store_root() / \"locks\"`, and\n`rebar._snapshot.repo_snapshot.store_root()` resolves to `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` **or else\n`tempfile.gettempdir()`**. On a developer box with `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` unset that is a single\ndirectory shared by **every worktree, every session and every process on the machine**. The\nfour `gate-slot-N` files in it are therefore a HOST-GLOBAL semaphore, not a per-suite or\nper-worktree one.\n\nTwo consequences:\n\n1. The slots can be exhausted by processes that are **running no tests at all**.\n2. Admission **fails closed WITHOUT waiting** — `_acquire_slot` returns `None` and the caller\n   raises immediately (`gate_admission.py:305`, \":class:`GateCongestedError` without waiting\n   when every slot is taken\"). So a test needing a slot dies instantly rather than queueing\n   behind the holder. Serialising the test run does not help; only freeing a slot does.\n\n## Proof: who actually held the slots\n\nTaken live with `lsof` on the four slot files while my own pytest count was **zero**:\n\n| slot | PID | holder cwd | process |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `gate-slot-0` | 50765 | `/Users/joeoakhart/janitor-e54e-shims` | `rebar verify-completion` |\n| `gate-slot-1` | 6229 | `/Users/joeoakhart/janitor-f773-cli` | `rebar review-plan` |\n| `gate-slot-2` | 20256 | `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar` | global `rebar-dev` release build |\n| `gate-slot-3` | 89566 | `/Users/joeoakhart/janitor-038d-config` | `rebar` gate op |\n\nAll four were **other sessions' real 15-20 minute LLM gate operations**, in four different\nworktrees. None was a test. None was mine. That is why the failures survived isolation, and\nit is the part that a \"concurrent xdist workers exhaust the suite's own slots\" framing does\nnot predict: the exhausting processes need not be running the suite, or any suite.\n\n## Scope: 31 tests across 9 files\n\nThis is not one test. Observed failing under contention:\n\n- `tests/unit/test_plan_review_retry.py` (16)\n- `tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py` (6 under isolation; 1 in the full run)\n- `tests/unit/test_plan_review_cli_retry.py` (3, knock-on `assert 11 == 2`)\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_peak_rss_9ea3.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_error_sidecar_heldout.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_eval_solver.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_error_sidecar.py` (1)\n\nThis directly answers AC4 of `torrential-unwhite-snail` (`9c2e-b44c-119e-4105`), which asked\nfor \"a check that no other test in the suite has the same host-wide coupling, or a ticket\nfiled for any that do\". They do; this is that ticket.\n\n## CI consequence\n\nThese tests are red whenever four real gate ops are in flight anywhere on the same machine —\n**including in CI if a runner is ever shared, or if a self-hosted runner also hosts gate\nwork**. The failure names gate congestion, so it reads as an infrastructure problem rather\nthan a test defect, which is exactly the shape that gets `recheck`ed instead of fixed. Per\nAGENTS.md that makes it a bug to root-cause, not a retry candidate: it is reproducible by\nconstruction (occupy all four slots, run the tests), not random.\n\n## Proposed fix direction\n\nGive the test suite its **own** slot directory rather than the host's, by pointing\n`REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` at a per-session temp dir in the test fixture. That is a one-line\nenvironment change at the fixture level and needs no change to `gate_admission`'s logic, so\nit keeps the production semantics (a genuinely shared host semaphore) exactly as they are\nwhile removing the cross-session coupling from the tests.\n\n**Not implemented here deliberately.** It touches the gate-admission path that several agent\nsessions are exercising concurrently right now, and the change that surfaced it was about\n`user_data.sh` mounts. Keeping them separate.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 - The coupling is reproduced deterministically: occupy all 4 host slots from a\n      process that runs no tests, then run the 9 files above and observe the same failures.\n      This must be a real reproduction, not an assumption from the field evidence.\n- [ ] AC2 - The listed tests pass with all four HOST slots held by an unrelated process.\n- [ ] AC3 - What each test actually asserts is still asserted. The fix must not be skipping,\n      deleting, or `xfail`ing them, and must not weaken gate admission itself.\n- [ ] AC4 - Production semantics are unchanged: a real gate op on a real host still contends\n      for a shared, host-wide semaphore. The isolation applies to the TEST suite only.\n- [ ] AC5 - Some guard stops a future test re-acquiring the host-global slot silently, so the\n      class does not simply grow back.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","9c2e-b44c-119e-4105"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"846b-4b51-0254-48fd","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gate admission's 4 slots are HOST-GLOBAL (store_root()/locks under tempfile.gettempdir()), so ~31 unit tests across 9 files go red whenever any process on the box holds a real gate op","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d11e286c-1c72-4216-bd7b-9d01028c2bb5","086e817d-62d8-4625-a962-abcd62512c73","3d38cc66-c82b-4a1d-9f9b-f642a3329ca0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788594160029011001,"uuid":"b043e980-f4d4-45fd-bb76-de7abf50aef6"}